`statusValueToStoryIdsMap` is initialised with only the five `TestStatusValue` keys. If any entry in `allStatuses` has `status.value` equal to `'status-value:new'`, `'status-value:modified'`, or `'status-value:affected'` (set by another addon), the cast `status.value as TestStatusValue` silently produces a key that doesn't exist in the map. `statusValueToStoryIdsMap[nonExistentKey]` is `undefined`, so `.push(status.storyId)` throws a `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'push')` at runtime. The fix is to guard before pushing:
```ts
if (status.value in statusValueToStoryIdsMap) {
  statusValueToStoryIdsMap[status.value as TestStatusValue].push(status.storyId);
}
```
